<tr>
<td VALIGN=TOP WIDTH="15%"><!-- Add marginal notes below --><i>Analysis
of a 2<sup>5-1</sup> Fractional Factorial Design</i></td>

<td VALIGN=TOP WIDTH="85%"><!-- Add main text below -->This case study
demonstrates the analysis of a 2<sup>5-1 </sup>fractional factorial design.
<p>This case study is a Dataplot analysis of the <a href="../section4/pri472.htm">catapult
data</a> discussed in the analysis section. The analysis section analyzed
the data using the JMP software.
<p>This case study will complement the material in the <a href="../section4/pri411.htm">analysis
chapter</a> by showing some additional graphical and analytical techniques
for analyzing fractional factorial experiments.Although different software
packages may provide somewhat different tools and techniques for analyzing
data from designed experiments, the fundamental goals are the same. That
is, we want to identify the important factors, determine best settings
for these factors, and find a good prediction equation using the important
factors.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td VALIGN=TOP WIDTH="15%"><!-- Add marginal notes below --><i>Contents</i></td>

<td VALIGN=TOP WIDTH="85%"><!-- Add main text below -->The case study is
divided into the following sections:
<ol>&nbsp;
<li>
<a href="pri621.htm">Background and data</a>&nbsp;</li>

<li>
<a href="pri622.htm">Main effects</a>&nbsp;</li>

<li>
<a href="pri623.htm">Interaction effects</a>&nbsp;</li>

<li>
<a href="pri624.htm">Estimate main and interaction effects</a>&nbsp;</li>

<li>
<a href="pri625.htm">Model selection criterion</a>&nbsp;</li>

<li>
<a href="pri626.htm">Best settings</a>&nbsp;</li>

<li>
<a href="pri627.htm">Conclusions and next step</a></li>
</ol>
</td>
</tr>

   
